    "profile": {
      "items": [
        {
          "type": "HTML",
          "html": "<B>Wisden obituary</B><BR>\nDon Pringle, was killed in a car crash on October 4 on his way back from a match in Nairobi, in which he had taken 6 for 16. He was 43. An opening bowler, he was one of the East African side in England last summer. He was unable, owing to injury, to play in the Prudential Cup match against New Zealand, but played against England, without, however, much success. Born in Lancashire, he had been playing for Kenya, where he was a landscape consultant, for seventeen years.\n<BR><B>Wisden Cricketers' Almanack</B>"
        }
      ]
    },
